{"skill":{"slug":"bear-notes","displayName":"Bear Notes"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1767545298356,"changelog":"","changelogSource":null,"license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":2454,"sha256":"d1d8b653e4d71a6450d9c3f2a9c2bf637ad8ae59a73e2a42830cff6f76977937","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1800,"sha256":"d43418e6f77f71bccda6817fcdbc8a4a81066ef7e210ce077362560efb08edb4","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789013571440,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"e8ec23687cf150ee061347ac5c76755aa1355ff57e435acf6140624a8447d4c6","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/e8ec23687cf150ee061347ac5c76755aa1355ff57e435acf6140624a8447d4c6","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: bear-notes\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe skill bundle is classified as benign. It provides instructions to install and use the `grizzly` CLI tool to manage Bear notes on macOS. The `SKILL.md` outlines the installation of `grizzly` via `go install` from a specific GitHub repository, and details how to interact with the Bear app, including handling user-provided API tokens stored in `~/.config/grizzly/token` and using local network callbacks (e.g., `127.0.0.1:42123`) for inter-process communication with Bear. All file and network access capabilities are explicitly tied to the stated purpose of managing Bear notes and do not show evidence of data exfiltration, malicious execution, persistence, or prompt injection attempts against the agent.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779159606235},"skillspector":{"status":"clean","normalizedStatus":"clean","score":9,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"SAFE","issueCount":1,"checkedAt":1789013571440},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill is a straightforward Bear notes helper, with manageable cautions around storing a Bear token locally and installing an unpinned third-party CLI.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The macOS-only scope, Bear app requirement, and grizzly dependency are proportionate to controlling Bear notes locally.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The skill installs the third-party grizzly CLI from github.com/tylerwince/grizzly/cmd/grizzly@latest, which is purpose-aligned but not pinned to an immutable reviewed version.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"Runtime instructions are user-invoked Bear note operations with clear examples; there are no hidden role changes, prompt overrides, background agents, or unrelated actions in the artifact.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The skill documents a plaintext Bear API token file and optional grizzly config under the user's home directory; this is expected for the integration but should be protected with restrictive permissions.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is to create, read, search, and manage Bear notes, and the documented grizzly commands directly match that purpose.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Before installing, treat the Bear token as sensitive: restrict access to ~/.config/grizzly/token, avoid sharing or backing it up broadly, and consider reviewing or pinning the grizzly CLI version instead of relying on @latest.","findings":"[SQP-2] expected: The plaintext token file is a real credential-handling caution, but it is disclosed and directly tied to Bear operations that require authentication.\n[T08] expected: The unpinned grizzly CLI dependency is a supply-chain risk, but the artifact contains no embedded payload, persistence mechanism, obfuscation, or unrelated execution behavior.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789013571440}}}}}